# ─── Dependencies ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Restored with `npm ci` from package-lock.json, which IS committed.
node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions


# ─── Build output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Regenerated by `npm run build`. Includes every optimised image variant, so
# committing it would add tens of megabytes that change on every build.
dist/
.output/
.vercel/
.netlify/


# ─── Astro generated ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Type definitions and the content cache, regenerated on dev/build.
.astro/


# ─── Visual QA artefacts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Screenshots captured during review — ~64 MB and reproducible at any time with
# `node apps/web/scripts/qa-shots.mjs`. Never useful in history.
qa/


# ─── Strapi (apps/cms) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Build output, caches and the admin bundle — all regenerated by `npm run build`
# inside apps/cms.
apps/cms/.tmp/
apps/cms/.strapi/
apps/cms/.cache/
apps/cms/build/
apps/cms/dist/
apps/cms/.strapi-updater.json

# ⚠ DO NOT ADD A BARE `apps/cms` LINE HERE. One was present until 2026-08-26 and
# it silently ignored the ENTIRE Strapi application — every content-type schema,
# every seed script, every config file. The CMS is source code and belongs in
# git; only the generated output above and the secrets and uploads below do not.

# ⚠⚠ UPLOADED MEDIA IS NOT VERSIONED, AND THAT IS THE DESIGN.
# Decision D5: images live on disk and are served by Caddy, not committed. This
# directory is school photography uploaded through the admin panel — it is
# backed up with the disk and the database, NOT with git. Committing it would
# recreate exactly the 199 MB-in-history problem the CMS migration exists to
# solve, and it would grow without limit.
apps/cms/public/uploads/*
!apps/cms/public/uploads/.gitkeep


# ─── Environment & secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key


# ─── Logs & caches ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
.npm/
.eslintcache
.cache/
*.tsbuildinfo


# ─── Test / tooling ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
coverage/
playwright-report/
test-results/
.playwright/


# ─── Editor & OS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# Windows
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# macOS
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*


# ─── OneDrive ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This project lives inside a synced OneDrive folder; these are sync leftovers.
*.tmp
~$*


# ─── Licensed fonts we do not have the right to redistribute ─────────────────
# ⚠ NOT A FREE FONT, WHATEVER THE DOWNLOAD SITE SAID. The file's own metadata
# reads "Copyright (c) 1989, 1990, 1991 Adobe Systems Incorporated. All Rights
# Reserved. Linotext is a trademark of Linotype-Hell AG"; the fontsgeek.com
# readme beside it grants no licence at all. Committing it would put an
# unlicensed commercial face into the repository's history, where removing it
# later means rewriting history. The site does not load it — see C11 in
# docs/07-client-asset-requests.md — and the wordmark it would have set is
# already artwork at public/brand/sunbeam-wordmark.png.
apps/web/src/assets/Linotext Regular/


# ─── Deliberately NOT ignored ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Keep these tracked — they are the project, not build output:
#
#   apps/web/src/assets/photos/  school photography the build imports/optimises
#   apps/web/public/brand/       logo derivatives from scripts/logo-prep.mjs
#   apps/web/public/fonts/       self-hosted variable WOFF2 files
#   apps/web/scripts/            logo prep + visual QA tooling
#   apps/cms/src/api/            Strapi content-type schemas — authored in the
#                                admin UI in development, but committed. They
#                                are the schema's source of truth and the
#                                content-type builder is disabled in production.
#   apps/cms/types/generated/    Strapi's generated TS types, so apps/web can
#                                typecheck the content contract without Strapi
#                                running.
#   docs/                        the approved design/requirements knowledge base
#   package-lock.json            ONE lockfile, at the repo root. The workspaces
#                                have none — npm hoists from here.
#   .env.example                 the environment template; .env itself is not
#   *.pdf                        the client audit report — governing requirements

# Strapi development lock — one instance per database (docs/09)
apps/cms/.strapi-develop.lock

# Database dumps and media archives — recovery artefacts, never source (docs/11).
# The uploads tarball alone is 335 MB.
backups/

# ⚠⚠ HERO VIDEO MASTERS — NEVER COMMIT THESE.
# src/assets/videos/*.MP4 are ~55 MB 1080p50 clips. An earlier pair were ~100 MB
# and one exceeded GitHub's 100 MB hard limit, which rejects the push outright.
# Only the encoded public/video/*.mp4 (1–3.7 MB) ship. The posters beside them
# ARE committed — they are the still every slide falls back to.
apps/web/src/assets/videos/*.MP4
apps/web/src/assets/videos/*.mp4
apps/web/src/assets/videos/*.mov
apps/web/src/assets/videos/*.MOV
